Upgrade procedure for libpcap

Source: https://www.tcpdump.org/release/libpcap-VERSION.tar.xz
	(check libpcap-VERSION.tar.xz.sig, signed by The Tcpdump Group,
	1F166A5742ABB9E0249A8D30E089DEF1D9C15D0D;
	https://www.tcpdump.org/release/signing-key.asc)

The vendor branch (vendor/libpcap) carries the complete release
tarball, and nothing is pruned in contrib/libpcap.

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download and verify the tarball and extract it into a new directory.
2. Use the vendor-update skill (vendor/libpcap, contrib/libpcap, tag
   vendor/libpcap/VERSION).  Stage with "git add -A -f".
3. Merge and re-apply the local patches below if they conflict.
4. Update lib/libpcap/Makefile and lib/libpcap/config.h.  FreeBSD's
   copies are a good reference; ours are otherwise identical to
   FreeBSD's.
5. Copy the new pcap/dlt.h to sys/net/dlt.h, changing FreeBSD to
   MidnightBSD throughout ("sed s/FreeBSD/MidnightBSD/g" on FreeBSD's
   sys/net/dlt.h reproduces ours exactly).  libpcap needs the new DLT_
   values, and both headers are included by programs using pcap.
6. Build lib/libpcap and usr.sbin/tcpdump (update tcpdump afterwards
   if it has a new release too).

Local patches applied on top of upstream (from FreeBSD, with FreeBSD
changed to MidnightBSD):

  - pcap/bpf.h: use the system <net/bpf.h> instead of libpcap's own
    BPF definitions (FreeBSD 6d1c946e9168).
  - pcap/pcap.h: remote capture is disabled.

Local patches applied on top of upstream (MidnightBSD):

  - pcap/dlt.h, pcap-bpf.c, pcap-netmap.c, pcap.c, pflog.h: test
    __MidnightBSD__ instead of __FreeBSD__.  Our compilers define
    both, so this changes no code, but it keeps pcap/dlt.h testing the
    same macro as sys/net/dlt.h.

Notes:
  - sys/net/dlt.h keeps FreeBSD's _NET_DLT_H_ include guard, so a
    program that includes both dlt.h headers processes both.  That is
    safe only while both test __MidnightBSD__ and agree on the DLT_
    values (DLT_PFSYNC 121, DLT_SLIP_BSDOS 13, DLT_PPP_BSDOS 14).
  - The CVE-2025-11961 backport to nametoaddr.c (1d2d357a0e) was
    replaced by the upstream fix in 1.10.6.
